proper professional production grade project structure setup :-
done by creating the folders inside the src:-
-controllers:- it'll contain our functionality 
-db:- it'll contain how to connect the db, the db connection logic is written here
-middlewares:- it'll contain the code that's run in between ie. the request that we've received, before the server fulfills that request, if we wanna put some checking in between then we do it inside the middleware, eg:- we've got a request and we're asking some info to the server, middlewares can be used in between and take the cookies from it so that we can know that if we're capable of taking that info or not 
-models:- it'll hv the schema of the db
-routes:-till now we'd used the routes(app.get, /instagram, /twitter etc) inside the index.js file only but professionally we need to use them inside the routes folder
-utils:-shortcut for the utility, while working we'll need a lot of utilities eg:- file upload is a utility and it'll be done in the form of the user profile, videos and many other forms as well so we make its utility, at many places, we'll use the mailing as well, we may also do the works of some tokens as well
so whatever work we're repeating that's kept inside the file/folder and we call it as utility whenever we need that file we use it 


