whenever we upload a file we need 2 packages at the backend:- express fileupload https://www.npmjs.com/package/express-fileupload and multer here we'll use multer https://www.npmjs.com/package/multer

THE STRATEGY THAT WE'RE GONNA USE FOR THE FILE UPLOADS:- 
1 we'll upload the file via the multer only as the file upload doesn't take place via cloudinary directly, cloudinary is only a service like the aws, it's an sdk 
cloudinary takes the file from us and uploads it on their server (either aws or cloudinary) 
2 we're gonna take the file from the user and store it on our local server temporarily 
3 in the next step, we'll use cloudinary to take the file from our local storage and will store it on the server
we can directly take the file from the multer and give it to the cloudinary to upload but in production grade settings the file is taken from the user and is stored on our local server temprarily so that when the file has come on our local server so that there can be chances of reupload 


